      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Onto our feature. Only six horses but the quality is there. JIMMYSSTAR (1) beat ANGEL CAPITAL in this race last year, arguably his best win to date although his form since has been a bit mixed. The Manikato win was impressive but he didn't beat a whole lot there, The Everest run was solid and he had no chance from the gate in the Russell Balding so excuses can be made. PERICLES (2) won the Russell Balding under a sweet ride. He's a G1 winner this trip and might be on fresher legs. The wet track advantages him. BEIWACHT (5) is the 1400m G1 specialist. He might not get all favours with SHADHAVAR (8) kicking up inside him but he did belt ANGEL CAPITAL & Jimmy in the Memsie earlier this Spring.",
